message: "If you use this software or empirical evaluation suite in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Chronodynamic Relativity: Unified Relativistic & Cosmological Empirical Evaluation Framework"
authors:
  - family-names: "Shreve"
    given-names: "Joshua A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5942-5351"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
license: "MIT"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshreve/Chronodynamic-Relativity"
keywords:
  - "cosmology"
  - "dark matter"
  - "dark energy"
  - "cosmic microwave background"
  - "baryon acoustic oscillations"
  - "sparc rotation curves"
  - "bullet cluster"
  - "relativistic gravitation"
abstract: >-
  Chronodynamic Relativity is a first-principles theoretical framework unifying cosmological expansion,
  galactic rotation curves, and early-universe acoustic scales without fine-tuned cold dark matter or
  cosmological constant parameters. This repository provides the official empirical evaluation suite,
  Boltzmann numerical solvers, observational data loaders, and reproduction pipelines across 1,930
  observational data points spanning four fundamental empirical pillars.
